WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.620
. . . believe, part of the destruction of Fitzgerald, I’m sorry to say, but Fitzgerald had . . . um . . . Popeyes.

2
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.620
Okay, that’s a big one.

3
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.680
And they were very unhappy with him, and Popeyes was very unhappy with that.

4
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.160
So, they fired him, and there was a period where they had no agency.

5
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:29.960
So I wrote a letter to the advertising director, who I didn’t know.

6
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.280
I said, “Can we talk?”

7
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:31.800
That was the only—

8
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.000
“Can we talk.”

9
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.340
—thing in my letter, “Can we talk?”

10
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:41.820
And he had an underling call and come visit us, and we pitched the account.

11
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:49.800
How we did it was, I had a young lady who was . . . very ambitious,

12
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.620
very sharp, who was going to be the account exec on this.

13
00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:01.040
I said, “Got to visit every Popeyes location in the area.”

14
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:14.260
So she went out and I went out and talked to each manager of Popeyes, and played back their input at the presentation.

15
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:19.420
“We’re not getting enough radio, we want more local newspaper.”

16
00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:26.520
All the things that they bitched about, or complimented, and we got the account.
